  "outcome": "The Delivery tab shows the project's six delivery lines from the live overview",
  "state": "IMPLEMENTING",
  "task_ids": [
    "FE-CONNECT-1"
  ],
  "operation_ids": [],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "`GET /projects/{uuid}/delivery-overview` is requested exactly once when `/projects/{uuid}/delivery` opens \u2014 verify: network log on Next 4990 (proxied to Django 8030) shows one request, 200.",
    "Six rows appear in the order release, go-live, hypercare, handover, archive, closure, even when the fixture returns them shuffled \u2014 verify: unit test on `deliveryModel.ts` with shuffled lines; page shows 01 to 06 in order.",
    "A started row shows title, reference, state tag and \"Updated <date>\", and \"Open\" goes to `/work/{work_id}` \u2014 verify: mock 4991 project P-0101, click Open on Release gates, URL is `/work/<id>`.",
    "A not-started row shows NOT STARTED with no reference, no date and no link, and no \"0\" or \"Unknown\" placeholder text in those slots \u2014 verify: second fixture project (all six `not_started`); page text contains no link in any row.",
    "Every `state` value in the contract maps to the table's tag text; an unlisted value shows UNKNOWN \u2014 verify: unit test over all 11 states plus null plus a made-up value.",
    "The page does not show \"of 6 done\", a DLV file number, gate wording such as \"RELEASE READY\", or a Tola check or \"Next\" sentence \u2014 verify: page text search on the P-0101 fixture finds none.",
    "With closure not started and `ready_to_prepare: false`, the closure row lists the title (and `finding`) of each held, unknown or unavailable check and nothing from current/closed/recorded checks \u2014 verify: component test with a checklist fixture.",
    "With `ready_to_prepare: true`, or when release-register or closure-checklist fails (403, 500, network), no closure reason shows and the six overview rows still show \u2014 verify: component test for each.",
    "The closure checklist is not requested when the release row has no `work_id` or when closure has a `work_id` \u2014 verify: test asserts no checklist call.",
    "403 and 404 on the overview show the same no-access panel with no project name or server message \u2014 verify: open `/projects/<P-0099 id>/delivery` on mock 4991.",
    "A 500 or network failure shows the error panel; \"Try again\" re-reads once and recovers \u2014 verify: component test with a failing then succeeding mock.",
    "A response with the wrong shape (missing key, five lines, duplicated key, unknown key) shows the error state, not a partial list \u2014 verify: unit test on the response check.",
    "The page makes no POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE and contains no start, edit or assign control \u2014 verify: grep `DeliveryTab.tsx`, `useDeliveryOverview.ts` for non-GET calls; none.",
    "Mobile width (390px) shows the six rows stacked without horizontal scroll \u2014 verify: browser at 390px on Next 4990.",
    "`src/features/workspace/**` and every path in `delivery/config.json` `protected_paths` have no changes \u2014 verify: `git diff --stat origin/main` lists neither.",
    "New tests exist for the model, the hook (race: a late answer for an earlier project is ignored) and the tab states, and `src/api/live-schema.d.ts` is unchanged \u2014 verify: `git diff --stat`, test files present."
  ],
  "risk": {
    "level": "low",
    "surfaces": [
      "ui",
      "api"
    ],
    "rated_by": "readiness",
    "rationale": "Low: a read-only screen on one new endpoint, with no money, identity, migration or sensitive data. It follows the existing line adapter pattern, and the only cross-layer contract is the overview response shape, which the live contract fixes. Surfaces are ui and api. Product acceptance is required because the overview flow and copy change from the mock. It can merge under D-180/D-184 once the build is on F-85."
  },
